#   square goodness-of-fit test against equal frequencies (1/6 each), reporting chi-
#   square(5) and p.
# Source quote:
#   "Bears were drawn without replacement and eaten, so the realized flavor frequencies
#   reflect package composition and sampling jointly: apple was administered on 23 trials,
#   orange, raspberry, and lemon on 17 each, pineapple on 15, and strawberry on 11. A
#   goodness-of-fit test against equal frequencies did not reject uniformity, ?�(5) = 4.52,
#   p = .477."
# Inputs: inputs/gummibear_trials.csv
# Depends on: A01, L01
# Produces: T158, T159
true_counts = trials["true_flavor"].value_counts().reindex(FLAVORS, fill_value=0)
exp_t = len(trials) / 6
chi2_gof = float(((true_counts.to_numpy() - exp_t) ** 2 / exp_t).sum())
